    "helps_anywhere": false,
    "statement": "The full SAGE-HE architecture never *materially* outperforms its own EfficientNet-B0 backbone at any training-set size measured. It is materially worse at 5% (-4.08 pts); at 10% (+0.55 pts) the gap falls inside the seed-to-seed spread and changes sign across seeds, because both arms are approaching the dataset's ceiling. The proposed components are therefore clearly harmful when labelled data is scarce, and indistinguishable from the bare backbone once it is not. No measured regime shows a reliable benefit."
